{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# ε → 0 (untwisting) structure of the finite-twist even-bridge identity (2026-10-13)\n\nAgent C of `notes/plan-2026-10-13.md` / `notes/w-a-reference-status.md` §4. **Full write-up: `notes/agent-2026-10-13-epsilon-expansion.md`.**\n\n> **STATUS.** Sections 0–3 (below) were first obtained in python (`checks/session-2026-10-13/epsexp/`) while the shared kernel was down ([num]/[exact] tags); the **port to wolfbook** (the section \"PORT TO WOLFBOOK\" at the end, tag **[wb]**) re-verifies items (1)–(5): step 0a, the T₁₄ identities, K₁ = 2−A−B−C with A·C = 4, the exact ω₂ formula and C_{M=1} = −1/√40, 1/√24 at L = 2, and the six L = 3 [1,0,1] states. Evidence tags: **[wb]** this notebook (exact rational unless stated), **[exact]** python `fractions`, **[num]** complex128 python, **[op]** operator identity on random vectors (1e-16). The ε-scans etc. remain python-only (see the summary cell at the end).\n\nConventions (README): chain A F A F …, site 1 leftmost = most significant tensor index, bras = row vectors, ψ → ψ·M; ℒ_s(u) = Σ e_ij ⊗ ((u−θ_s)δ_ij + hρ_s(E_ij)), ρ_A(E_ij) = e_ij, ρ_F(E_ij) = −e_ji, h = ½; T = ℒ₁…ℒ_N, twist on the right; fused one-pass t_k (aux ∧^k); W_a = (e₁+ae₄)⊗(e₄−ae₁); J = ρ(E₁₄) (global), ⟨W_a^L| = ⟨vac^L|e^{aJ}; T₁₄ = tr(T E₄₁).\nUntwisting: z = 1+εφ (φ₂=φ₃), κ = 1−cε, a = (φ₁−c)/(φ₁−φ₄), θ_F,n = εθ⁰_n, θ_A = θ_F+2h; Ψ_ε → HW state Ψ₀ (unit norm, ⟨vac|vac⟩ = 1).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 0. Step 0a — exact at L = 2 [exact; `step0a.py`]\n\nθ = (2/7, −3/5, 8/11, −11/8), z = (3/2, 5/4, 2/3, 4/7), a = 1/3, u ∈ {1/5, −2/3, 3/7}, k = 1, 2, 3.\n\n| twist G | ⟨W_a^L\\|t_k^G(u) ∝ ⟨W_a^L\\| ? | eigenvalue |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Λ + a(z₁−z₄)E₄₁** | **yes, all (k,u)** | **= τ_vac,k(u)** |\n| Λ + a(z₄−z₁)E₄₁ | no | – |\n| Λ (a ≠ 0) | no | – |\n| Λ + ((z₄−z₁)/a)E₁₄ | yes | ≠ τ_vac (the e₄⊗e₁ vacuum) |\n| Λ + ((z₁−z₄)/a)E₁₄ | no | – |\n\n* G_a = e^{aE₄₁} Λ e^{−aE₄₁} [exact]; t^{G_a} = t^Λ + a(z₁−z₄)T₁₄. ⟨vac\\| is not an eigenbra of t^{G_a}.\n* Companion frame (V = columns (z_j³,z_j²,z_j,1)): VΛV⁻¹ = G_c(z) but V⁻¹ΛV ≠ G_c, so the frame image is **V G_a V⁻¹ = G_c(z) + a(z₁−z₄) v(z₄)⊗ũ₁** (v(z₄) = (z₄³,z₄²,z₄,1)ᵀ, ũ₁ = row 1 of V⁻¹; rank-one, exact). The literal V⁻¹G_aV is not the companion-frame image. For a ≠ 0 the image is not a companion matrix (as found before). Numeric matrices: `out_step0a.txt`.\n* Operator identities [op 1e-16, finite ε, generic θ]: **[J, t₁^Λ(u)] = −(z₁−z₄)T₁₄(u)**, [J, T₁₄(u)] = 0. Together with the eigenbra property: **(τ_vac(u) − τ_Ψ(u))⟨W_a^L\\|Ψ⟩ = a(z₁−z₄)⟨W_a^L\\|T₁₄(u)\\|Ψ⟩** for every eigenstate Ψ of t^Λ, any u, any finite ε [num: ≤ 2e-6 (L=2), ≤ 5e-6 (L=3, n ≤ 2)].",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. Orders in ε, the product formula, K₁ [num; `scan_eps.py`, `scan2.py`, `an3.py`, `kspec.py`]\n\nK := K_κ(τ_{Ψε}), w := ⟨W_a^L\\|Ψ_ε⟩, LHS := ⟨W_{a′}⊗W_a^{L−1}\\|Ψ_ε⟩ = K w/N, N = (1−κz₁)² ~ ε² (identity exact to ≤1e-6 everywhere). n := L − μ₁ for weight (μ₁,0,0,−μ₁); **w ≡ 0 for every other weight**; ⟨W_a\\|Ψ⟩ = (aⁿ/n!)⟨vac\\|Jⁿ\\|Ψ⟩.\n\n| L | state | n | K₁ | slopes (w, K, LHS) | Richardson K w/N | data C_{M=1} |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2,3 | vacuum | 0 | 0 | (0, 2, 0) | 0.9999996 | 1 |\n| 2 | [1 0 1]×2 | 1 | 0 | (1, 2, 1) | 0 | 0 |\n| 3 | [2 0 2]×3 | 1 | 0 | (1, 2, 1) | 0 | 0 |\n| 2 | [0 0 0]×2 | 2 | 10, 2 | (2, 0, 0) | −0.1581144, 0.2041241 | −0.1581139, 0.2041241 |\n| 3 | [1 0 1]×6 | 2 | 3.657, −7.657, 14.658(×2), 1.842(×2) | (2, 0, 0) | −0.1711261, −0.0271378, −0.0358717∓0.0286379i, 0.1299242∓0.0817131i | −0.1711264, −0.0271377, −0.0358717∓0.0286375i, 0.1299243∓0.0817131i |\n| 3 | [0 0 0]×4 | 3 | 7.5, 7.5, −22.65, 2.65 | (3, 0, 1) | 0 (±4e-7) | 0 |\n| 2,3 | other weights | – | −12 … 8 (≠ 0) | w ≡ 0 | 0 | 0 |\n\n**Findings.**\n1. *K₁ = 0 for every non-vacuum state is false.* K₁ = 0 on the irreps [L,0,L] (n=0) and [L−1,0,L−1] (n=1) (forced there: K w/N finite with w = O(εⁿ) gives K = O(ε^{2−n})); non-zero on the others. Whole-sector spectra (all eigenstates): L=2 zero-weight sector, 28 states, K₁ ≠ 0 on exactly 4 (10, 2, 8, 8); L=3 sectors (2,0,0,−2) and (1,0,0,−1): see `out_kspec_L3.txt`.\n2. *Product formula, corrected:* **C_{M=1}(Ψ₀) = K₁(τ_Ψ₀) · ω₂(Ψ₀)/(2(φ₁−φ₄)²)**, ω₂ := lim ε⁻²⟨vac\\|J²\\|Ψ_ε⟩, only n=2 states contribute (the lead's K′w′ is the n=1 case, where K′=0 and C=0).\n3. *Structure of K₁:* with A = τ_F/(h²λ₁), B = τ₂(u₀)/(2h⁴yλ₂), C = τ̂₃(u₀)/(6h⁵y²λ₃): **K_κ = s² + κs(A+B+C) + κ²AC/4**; at the untwisted point **AC = 4 for all 6 (L=2) + 26 (L=3) HW states** (τ_F τ̂₃(u₀) state-independent), so **K₁ = 2 − (A+B+C)**. Vacuum (2,−2,2), adjoints A+B+C = 2.\n4. *First-order data:* the shifts (A′,B′,C′) equal Hellmann–Feynman in the untwisted eigenbasis (5 digits; 5 states L=2, 8 states L=3); K′ = 0 for n ≤ 1 (nontrivial cancellation), K′ ≠ 0 for n ≥ 2 (not needed). Use the **normalised** A,B,C (λ₃ contains O(ε^{L−1}) factors at finite ε). Twisted-Q check of X′ **not done**.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. What w needs [num; `pt.py`, `pt2.py`]\n\nFrom [J,t^Λ] = −(z₁−z₄)T₁₄ and the eigenbra identity of §0 (matching orders in ε):\n\n**ωₙ (τ_vac(u) − τ_Ψ₀(u)) = n(φ₁−φ₄) lim ε^{−(n−1)}⟨vac\\|T₁₄(u)J^{n−1}\\|Ψ_ε⟩**, hence the twist enters only as (φ₁−φ₄)ⁿ (no φ₂,φ₃, θ⁰, c).\n\n* n=1: **ω₁ = (φ₁−φ₄)⟨vac\\|T₁₄(u)\\|Ψ₀⟩/(τ_vac(u)−τ_Ψ₀(u))** (u-independent; L=2 [1 0 1]: ±0.33333i; L=3 [2 0 2]: −0.204124(1±i), −0.204124).\n* n=2: first-order PT with JΨ₀ = 0, [J,V] = −(φ₁−φ₄)T₁₄(u₁) gives JΨ₁ = (φ₁−φ₄)(t₁(u₁)−τ_Ψ₀(u₁))⁻¹T₁₄(u₁)Ψ₀, so\n  **ω₂ = 2(φ₁−φ₄)² ⟨vac\\|T₁₄(u)(t₁(u₁)−τ_Ψ₀(u₁))⁻¹T₁₄(u₁)\\|Ψ₀⟩/(τ_vac(u)−τ_Ψ₀(u))** (all untwisted; any u, u₁; resolvent on the sector of JΨ₀) and\n  **C_{M=1}(Ψ₀) = K₁(τ_Ψ₀)⟨vac\\|T₁₄(u)(t₁(u₁)−τ_Ψ₀(u₁))⁻¹T₁₄(u₁)\\|Ψ₀⟩/(τ_vac(u)−τ_Ψ₀(u))**. Reproduces the data C_{M=1} to 6 digits at L=2 (−1/√40, 1/√24) and L=3 (six [1 0 1]); ω₂ values: L=2 −0.126491, 0.816497; L=3 −0.374369, 0.028354, −0.019578∓0.015630i, 0.564276∓0.354889i. (n=3 ladder with two resolvents: conjecture, untested.)\n* **Which states contribute.** First order (n=1): only the vacuum tower (τ = τ_vac; weight multiplicity 3 in [L,0,L] at (L−1)(e₁−e₄), 6 at n=2, 10 at n=3; ⟨vac\\|Jⁿ picks one combination). Second order (n=2): only the HW states of **[L−1,0,L−1]** (4 at L=2, 9 at L=3, cyclic or not) — K₁ vanishes on all of them. ⟨vac\\|J^k\\|Ψ_m⟩ = 0 for all k when m < n.\n* (4a) κ = 1/z₄ is the c = φ₄ member of the same family (a = 1, a′ = 0; with a = −1, no shift: M = L−1); same product, same unknown ω, only the symmetry C_M = (−1)^{L+μ₄}C_{L−M} — **no independent handle**.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. (4b) Even vs odd bridges [num; `scan2.py`, `odd_check.py`, `pt2.py`]\n\n* Odd-bridge chain (NEXT.md 2j): ⟨bra_ε\\|Ψ_ε⟩ = word_eig·⟨W_a^L\\|Ψ_ε⟩ exact to 1e-15 at finite ε (L=2,3; k=1 A-site, k=2 F-site, ABJM pair-preserving θ). Limit: ⟨bra_ε\\|Ψ_ε⟩/(ε(c+φ)) → (a∓a′)C₁ on [L−1,0,L−1], V₀ on the vacuum, 0 on the rest.\n* Hence **ω₁(m) = (φ₄−φ₁)C₁(m)/D₀(m)** (D₀ = ε→0 word eigenvalue: L=2 [1 0 1] 3/2 ± (√3/2)i, L=3 [2 0 2] 1±i, 2) and **κ_m := ⟨vac\\|T₁₄(u)\\|m⟩/(τ_vac(u)−τ_m(u)) = −C₁(m)/D₀(m)** [num 1e-4, 2+3 states, both k].\n* **No ratio relation at fixed state:** odd ℓ=1 sees n=1 states, even M=1 sees n=2 states; they are never both non-zero.\n* **Relation that exists (first-order PT):** C_{M=1}(Ψ) = K₁(τ_Ψ)/(τ_vac(u)−τ_Ψ(u)) · Σ_m κ_m (τ_vac(u)−τ_m(u)) g_m, g_m = ⟨m̃\\|T₁₄(u₁)\\|Ψ₀⟩/(τ_m(u₁)−τ_Ψ(u₁)), m over the HW states of [L−1,0,L−1]: **even n=2 data = K₁ × odd-bridge data of the adjoint-type states × a T₁₄ form factor ⟨m\\|T₁₄\\|Ψ⟩** (the new unknown, Slavnov-type; not a Q-bracket of Ψ alone).\n\n## 4. Not done / how to continue\n\n* No wolfbook run (kernel lost); WL port of `step0a.py` (exact), `scan2.py`/`pt2.py` (L=2) is straightforward once K1 is restored — use **memo-free** definitions and `SparseArray` products, test k=1 first (the draft that blew up cached a wrong `ueSite`).\n* X′ from twisted Q-functions: not done. ω₂ formula tested on cyclic HW Ψ₀ only; n ≥ 3 untested.\n* Files: `checks/session-2026-10-13/epsexp/` (`ue_base.py`, `ue2.py`, `scan_eps.py`, `scan2.py`, `an3.py`, `hf.py`, `pt.py`, `pt2.py`, `odd_check.py`, `kspec.py`, `step0a.py`, `out_*.txt`, `tables_C.txt`).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# PORT TO WOLFBOOK (kernel restored 08:03; prefix `ue`, no memoisation, Module-local SparseArrays)\n\nEverything below is computed in this notebook. Tag **[wb]** = verified in the kernel here (exact rational unless stated); the python-only statements stay tagged [num]/[py] in the cells above. Building blocks are tested on a 1-pair (2-site) chain first.\n\n### Building blocks\nFused one-pass transfer matrices `t_k^G(u) = ∏g · Σ_{I,J} (∧^k G)_{JI} T_{IJ}(u)`, aux = ∧^k C⁴; the monodromy blocks T_{IJ} are 4^N×4^N sparse matrices acting on bras (ψ → ψ·M, site 1 = most significant). `ueMono` builds all aux blocks by plain sparse products; `ueTG` contracts with any twist matrix G (so T₁₄ = t₁^{E₄₁}).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ue machinery: no memoisation; everything Module-local. psi -> psi.M convention, chain A F A F ..., site 1 most significant. *)\nueDKall[k_] := Module[{S = Subsets[Range[4], {k}], eps},\n   Table[Coefficient[Det[(IdentityMatrix[4] + eps Normal[SparseArray[{{a, b} -> 1}, {4, 4}]])[[ii, jj]]], eps, 1], {a, 4}, {b, 4}, {ii, S}, {jj, S}]];\nueSiteBlocks[k_, ty_] := Module[{n = Binomial[4, k], dk = ueDKall[k], rho},\n   rho = Table[If[ty === \"A\", SparseArray[{{a, b} -> 1}, {4, 4}], SparseArray[{{b, a} -> -1}, {4, 4}]], {a, 4}, {b, 4}];\n   Table[Plus @@ Flatten[Table[dk[[a, b, K, Kp]] rho[[a, b]], {a, 4}, {b, 4}], 1], {K, n}, {Kp, n}]];\nueGpref[k_, u_, types_, th_, h_, reg_] := Times @@ Flatten[Table[\n    Table[With[{f = u - th[[s]] - j h}, If[reg && f == 0, 1, f]], {j, If[types[[s]] === \"A\", Range[1, k - 1], Range[0, k - 2]]}], {s, Length[types]}]];\nueMono[k_, u_, types_, th_, h_] := Module[{nn = Length[types], n = Binomial[4, k], dim, id, zero, sb, T, tt, Lb},\n   dim = 4^nn; id = IdentityMatrix[dim, SparseArray]; zero = SparseArray[{}, {dim, dim}];\n   sb = <|\"A\" -> ueSiteBlocks[k, \"A\"], \"F\" -> ueSiteBlocks[k, \"F\"]|>;\n   T = Table[If[K == Kp, id, zero], {K, n}, {Kp, n}];\n   Do[tt = If[types[[s]] === \"A\", th[[s]], th[[s]] + (k - 1) h];\n    Lb = Table[If[K == Kp, (u - tt) id, zero] + h KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[4^(s - 1), SparseArray], sb[types[[s]]][[K, Kp]], IdentityMatrix[4^(nn - s), SparseArray]], {K, n}, {Kp, n}];\n    T = Table[Sum[T[[K, K2]] . Lb[[K2, Kp]], {K2, n}], {K, n}, {Kp, n}], {s, nn}];\n   T];\nueCompound[k_, G_] := With[{S = Subsets[Range[4], {k}]}, Table[Det[G[[ii, jj]]], {ii, S}, {jj, S}]];\nueTG[T_, k_, G_, pref_] := Module[{n = Binomial[4, k], W = ueCompound[k, G]},\n   pref Plus @@ Flatten[Table[If[W[[J1, I1]] === 0, 0 T[[I1, J1]], W[[J1, I1]] T[[I1, J1]]], {I1, n}, {J1, n}], 1]];\nueKronVec[vs_] := Flatten[Outer[Times, Sequence @@ vs]];\nueWpair[a_] := {{1, 0, 0, a}, {-a, 0, 0, 1}};\nueWbra[als_List] := ueKronVec[Flatten[ueWpair /@ als, 1]];\nueVacBra[Lp_] := ueKronVec[Flatten[Table[{{1, 0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 0, 1}}, {Lp}], 1]];\n{\"loaded\", MemoryInUse[]/10.^9}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"725116\" data-output-id=\"71\" data-out-n=\"424\" data-sub-idx=\"11\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"6\" data-sub-start=\"23\" data-sub-end=\"23\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[424]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"15\" data-latex-b64=\"XGxlZnRce1x0ZXh0e2xvYWRlZH0sMC44NzQ4MjY3MjAwMDAwMDAxXHJpZ2h0XH0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">loaded</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.8748267200000001</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
