3.3,1,-4c1.3,-2.7,23.83,-20.7,67.5,-54\nc44.2,-33.3,65.8,-50.3,66.5,-51c1.3,-1.3,3,-2,5,-2c4.7,0,8.7,3.3,12,10\ns173,378,173,378c0.7,0,35.3,-71,104,-213c68.7,-142,137.5,-285,206.5,-429\nc69,-144,104.5,-217.7,106.5,-221\nl0 -0\nc5.3,-9.3,12,-14,20,-14\nH400000v40H845.2724\ns-225.272,467,-225.272,467s-235,486,-235,486c-2.7,4.7,-9,7,-19,7\nc-6,0,-10,-1,-12,-3s-194,-422,-194,-422s-65,47,-65,47z\nM834 80h400000v40h-400000z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1272em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.538em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.2642em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:1.1138em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.9238em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:10.3476em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-4.9238em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.4238em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.4238em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.5676em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.4238em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.9676em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.4238em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.8076em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.4238em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-11.6476em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.4238em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-12.8476em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.4238em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.9238em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[479]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{singlet} & \\text{tau\\_F(theta\\_F)} & \\text{K1} & \\text{(u,u1)} & \\text{omega\\_2 (exact)} & \\text{omega\\_2 numeric} & \\text{C = K1 omega\\_2/(2 (phi1-phi4)\\^{}2)} & \\text{C\\_direct = <W\\_-1 x vac|Psi0>}\\\\\\hline1 & -\\frac{1}{4} & 2 & \\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{2}{5}\\right\\} & \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} & 0.81649658 & \\frac{1}{2\\,\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{2\\,\\sqrt{6}}\\\\\\hline &  &  & \\left\\{-\\frac{2}{3},-\\frac{1}{3}\\right\\} & \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} & 0.81649658 & \\frac{1}{2\\,\\sqrt{6}} & \\\\\\hline2 & \\sqrt{10}\\,\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}}}{16}-\\frac{1}{16\\,\\sqrt{10}}\\right) & 10 & \\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{2}{5}\\right\\} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{5}}}{5} & -0.12649111 & -\\frac{1}{2\\,\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{2\\,\\sqrt{10}}\\\\\\hline &  &  & \\left\\{-\\frac{2}{3},-\\frac{1}{3}\\right\\} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{5}}}{5} & -0.12649111 & -\\frac{1}{2\\,\\sqrt{10}} & \\\\\\hline\\text{data C\\_\\{M=1\\} (singlets, E = 20 and 4)} & \\left\\{-0.15811388300841894+0.\\,\\,\\mathrm{i},0.2041241452319302 +0.\\,\\,\\mathrm{i}\\right\\} &  &  &  &  &  & \\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "42a67ea8-42c3-44a9-99ec-0fb5d0f5cc54"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (4) [wb, exact]:** for the two L = 2 singlets (τ_F = ±1/4; K₁ = 10 and 2) the untwisted operator formula gives ω₂ = −(1/5)√(2/5) = −0.1264911 and √(2/3) = 0.8164966, independent of (u, u₁) (two pairs tested), and\n\n**C_{M=1} = K₁ω₂/(2(φ₁−φ₄)²) = −1/(2√10) = −1/√40 and +1/(2√6) = +1/√24 exactly**, equal to the direct overlap ⟨W_{−1}⊗vac|Ψ₀⟩ (and to the data C_{M=1} = −0.158114, 0.204124). The resolvent acts on the 12-dim weight sector (1,0,0,−1); the singlet space is 2-dim (kernel of E_ij for all 6 raising/lowering generators in the zero-weight sector).\n\n## (5) L = 3, six [1,0,1] states (weight sector (1,0,0,−1) → J-sector (2,0,0,−2), dim 24), machine precision [wb]\n\nAt 3 pairs the 4096-dim monodromy blocks are not built; instead t_k^G(u)ψ and T₁₄(u)ψ are applied **to vectors** by propagating the aux-block array Φ[I,J] = T_{IJ}ψ site by site (no matrices beyond 4×4 site blocks). First a building-block test against the exact 2-pair matrices.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* vector application of the fused monodromy: Phi[I,J] = T_IJ(u) psi, propagated site by site (machine numerics) ; tested against the exact sparse matrices at L = 2 *)\nueSiteApply[m_, s_, nn_, v_] := Flatten[Transpose[Transpose[ArrayReshape[v, {4^(s - 1), 4, 4^(nn - s)}], {1, 3, 2}] . Transpose[m], {1, 3, 2}]];\nueApplyBlocks[k_, u_, types_, th_, h_, psi_, rows_] := Module[{nn = Length[types], n = Binomial[4, k], sb, Phi, tt, dim = Length[psi], sbN},\n   sb = <|\"A\" -> Map[Normal, ueSiteBlocks[k, \"A\"], {2}], \"F\" -> Map[Normal, ueSiteBlocks[k, \"F\"], {2}]|>;\n   Phi = Table[If[I1 == J1, psi, ConstantArray[0. + 0. I, dim]], {I1, rows}, {J1, n}];\n   Do[tt = If[types[[s]] === \"A\", th[[s]], th[[s]] + (k - 1) h]; sbN = sb[types[[s]]];\n    Phi = Table[Sum[(u - tt) If[K == J1, 1, 0] Phi[[r, K]] + h ueSiteApply[N[sbN[[K, J1]]], s, nn, Phi[[r, K]]], {K, n}], {r, Length[rows]}, {J1, n}], {s, nn}];\n   Phi];\n(* t_k^G(u) psi  and  T_IJ(u) psi *)\nueApplyT[k_, G_, u_, types_, th_, h_, psi_, reg_] := Module[{n = Binomial[4, k], W = ueCompound[k, G], Phi},\n   Phi = ueApplyBlocks[k, u, types, th, h, psi, Range[n]];\n   ueGpref[k, u, types, th, h, reg] Sum[W[[J1, I1]] Phi[[I1, J1]], {I1, n}, {J1, n}]];\nueApplyTIJ[u_, types_, th_, h_, psi_, I0_, J0_] := ueApplyBlocks[1, u, types, th, h, psi, {I0}][[1, J0]];\n(* building-block test at L = 2: random vector, exact sparse matrices vs vector application, generic theta and z *)\nueTestVec = Module[{h = 1/2, types = {\"A\", \"F\", \"A\", \"F\"}, th = {2/7, -3/5, 8/11, -11/8}, z = {3/2, 5/4, 2/3, 4/7}, Lam, psi, errs, E41 = SparseArray[{{4, 1} -> 1}, {4, 4}]},\n  Lam = DiagonalMatrix[z]; SeedRandom[7]; psi = RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 256];\n  errs = Table[Module[{M = ueMono[k, 1/5, types, th, h]}, Max[Abs[ueTG[M, k, Lam, ueGpref[k, 1/5, types, th, h, False]] . psi - ueApplyT[k, Lam, 1/5, types, N[th], 0.5, psi, False]]]], {k, 3}];\n  Module[{M = ueMono[1, 1/5, types, th, h]}, AppendTo[errs, Max[Abs[ueTG[M, 1, E41, 1] . psi - ueApplyT[1, E41, 1/5, types, N[th], 0.5, psi, False]]]]];\n  Grid[{{\"max |matrix.psi - vector application|\", \"t1\", \"t2\", \"t3\", \"T14\"}, Prepend[ScientificForm[#, 2] & /@ errs, \"L = 2, generic theta, z\"]}, Frame -> All]];\n{ueTestVec /. Grid[g_, ___] :> g, MemoryInUse[]/10.^9}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
