   "value": "**Result (5) [wb, machine precision]:** for all six L = 3 [1,0,1] HW states (K₁ = 3.656854, −7.656854, 14.658003 (×2), 1.842 (×2), from X₁, X₂, X̂₃ eigenvalues on the data states; eigen-residual ≤ 1e-15) the untwisted operator formula (resolvent on the 24-dim sector (2,0,0,−2)) gives ω₂ and C_{M=1} = K₁ω₂/(2(φ₁−φ₄)²) = −0.171126, −0.027138, −0.035872∓0.028637i (× conj pair), 0.129924∓0.081713i (× conj pair); the same for both (u,u₁) pairs (3/7, 2/5) and (−2/3, −1/3), equal to the direct overlap ⟨W_{−1}⊗vac²|Ψ₀⟩ and to the data C_{M=1}: max deviation ≤ 8e-15. The ω₂ values are those of the python run (−0.374369, 0.028354, …).\n\n## Summary of the port\n\n**Ported and verified in this notebook [wb]:** (1) step 0a, exact at L = 2 (k = 1,2,3); (2a) t₁^{G_a} = t₁^Λ + a(z₁−z₄)T₁₄ exactly, (2b) the finite-twist identity on all 41 eigenstates of the three relevant sectors to 1e-29; (3) K₁ = 2 − A − B − C, A·C = 4 on the six HW states, exact K₁ characteristic polynomials, **new exact operator identity X̂₃X₁ = 24h⁷λ₁λ₃ P (P = pair translation)**, K₁ values 0, 0, 8, 10, 2; (4) C_{M=1} = −1/√40, 1/√24 exactly from K₁ω₂/(2(φ₁−φ₄)²) with the exact untwisted ω₂ formula; (5) the same at L = 3 for the six [1,0,1] states (machine precision, vector-applied monodromy).\n\n**Remain python-only [num]:** the ε-scans (orders in ε, Richardson limits, ω_n from ⟨vac|Jⁿ|Ψ_ε⟩, product formula at finite ε on the twisted eigenstates), Hellmann–Feynman and K′, the full K₁ spectra at L=3, the odd-bridge chain identity and κ_m = −C₁/D₀, the 26-state tables, A·C = 4 at L=3 (all in `checks/session-2026-10-13/epsexp/`). Not done at all: X′ from twisted Q-functions; n ≥ 3.",
